Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 22:14:45 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 078/130] shader: the stock casters' SKINNING and MORPHING
 combos compile
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three fixes, from the shader sweep's 10 caster failures (stock shadowcaster, shadowcasterfoliage4,
shadowcasterfur4 with SKINNING or MORPHING):

- SKINNING with BONECOUNT 0 declared g_Bones[0]. WE sets BONECOUNT to the skeleton's bone count
  whenever it sets SKINNING (GH 0x140230ec0, vtable +0xd8), so a SKINNING unit without a count
  gets 1.
- shadowcasterfoliage4 reads g_Texture1Texel under MORPHING and declares only
  g_Texture1Resolution. g_Texture0Texel … g_Texture9Texel are engine uniforms in WE's name table
  (GH 0x140002a20, ids 0x49–0x52). On glslang's "undeclared identifier" the unit now declares
  it, and CPass feeds g_Texture<n>Texel = (1 / width, 1 / height, width, height) for every bound
  texture. Inferred: that value, from model_vertex_v1.h's morph lookups (x = i % texel.z).
- shadowcasterfur4 passes gl_VertexID (an int) to ApplyMorphPosition (in uint vertexID). The
  call-argument rule now finds definitions whose parameter list holds a macro call
  (DECLARE_SAMPLER2D_PARAMETER (morphTexture)), and leaves array parameters alone.

Origin: ours
Why: docs/player/spikes/we-coverage.md F4 (the shadow-caster SKINNING / MORPHING sweep failures)
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
